From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1623/1623] SableOS: Manage Connections screen for BlackBerry 7

Owner board 2026-11-20. One dark list with a checkbox per radio: Turn All
Connections Off (airplane mode, reads Restore Connections when on), Mobile
Network with the carrier, Wi-Fi with the SSID, Bluetooth, NFC where present, then
links to Wi-Fi setup, Networks and Connections and Services Status. The shade
banner opens it with action org.sableos.settings.MANAGE_CONNECTIONS.
---
diff --git a/AndroidManifest.xml b/AndroidManifest.xml
index 5ff9a6a..3816b90 100644
--- a/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -3942,6 +3942,17 @@
             </intent-filter>
         </receiver>
 
+        <!-- SableOS: BlackBerry 7 Manage Connections, opened by the shade banner with the action alone. -->
+        <activity android:name=".sable.SableManageConnectionsActivity"
+            android:exported="true"
+            android:label="@string/sable_manage_connections_title"
+            android:theme="@android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault.DayNight">
+            <intent-filter>
+                <action android:name="org.sableos.settings.MANAGE_CONNECTIONS" />
+                <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
+            </intent-filter>
+        </activity>
+
         <!-- SableOS: Sable Audio, Bluetooth codec choices (Connected devices). -->
         <activity android:name=".sable.SableAudioActivity"
             android:exported="false"
